TITLE:: PianoRollLoopMarkers
SUMMARY:: Vertical loop start and stop lines on a piano roll.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/PianoRoll

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::PianoRollLoopMarkers:: holds two LINK::Classes/View:: instances (one beat wide). LINK::Classes/PianoRoll#-stopRecording:: calls LINK::#-loopBoundsInBeats_:: with the recorded note range. The LINK::Classes/GuiPalette:: passed to LINK::#-new:: is only used for the marker colour (LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5::) when the lines are first created.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::PianoRollLoopMarkers::. The line LINK::Classes/View::s are created on the first call to LINK::#-loopBoundsInBeats_::.

ARGUMENT:: parent
The roll surface (typically the piano roll LINK::Classes/UserView::) on which the lines are parented.

ARGUMENT:: horizontalScale
Pixels per beat, matching the roll's horizontal scale.

ARGUMENT:: rollHeight
Height of the lines in pixels (typically the full roll height).

ARGUMENT:: palette
A LINK::Classes/GuiPalette::; only LINK::Classes/GuiPalette#-colour5:: is kept for drawing the lines.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: loopBoundsInBeats_
Creates or updates the start and stop lines at the given beat positions.

ARGUMENT:: startBeat
Beat index for the loop start line.

ARGUMENT:: stopBeat
Beat index for the loop stop line.

PRIVATE:: init
